{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the `rate` service and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned 200, but I haven't seen the validation result.\n\n- **Cause:** The `rate` deployment had `RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT=20` and `RATE_QUEUE_CAPACITY=256` set. Those limits throttled it. `search` was logging `DeadlineExceeded` and `ResourceExhausted` errors on its calls to `rate`.\n- **Fix:** I removed both environment variables with `kubectl set env deploy/rate -n hotel-reservation RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT- RATE_QUEUE_CAPACITY-`. I didn't check what limits `rate` uses when they're unset.\n- **Check:** The rollout completed. Right after the restart, `search` logged some `Unavailable` errors from `rate`. Later checks of the last 15 seconds of `search` and `frontend` logs showed no errors, but that's a short window."}}
